# COMPONENT

## KnowledgeLake

### SUMMARY

Prepare and export evidence-grounded raw proposals from explicit local fixtures.

### DESCRIPTION

KnowledgeLake executes the project-local preparation flow using an explicit UTF-8 fixturePath and a fresh storeDirectory. It persists versioned Run, material and proposal lineage, writes JSON and Markdown exports, and returns the exact persisted report JSON in reportJson. Writes are side effects and expected failures retain structured local write outcomes. Fixture observations prove only local handling; live provider, receiving Candidate lifecycle, Admission and publication guarantees remain unverified.

### PACKAGE

org.simplemodeling.textus.knowledgelake

### USE CASE

#### propose_raw_knowledge_candidate

##### ID

UC-KA-01

##### PRIMARY ACTOR

KnowledgeWorker

##### SUPPORTING ACTOR

TextusKnowledgeWorkbench
ResourceProvider
KnowledgeProcessor

##### SUMMARY

Propose Raw Knowledge Candidate through project-local fixture/manual-result execution.

##### PRECONDITION

a valid UTF-8 local-flow v1 fixture, an empty explicit local store directory, versioned Resource/Evidence/Context and existing-information baseline, and explicitly supplied deterministic/manual preparation results and boundary observations.

##### POSTCONDITION

PreparedMaterial and a producer-scoped RawCandidateProposal are persisted with fixed Run/input/evidence lineage, local delivery observations are correlated, canonical JSON/Markdown/proposal exports exist, and the returned report describes actual persisted state. Fixture receipt/Candidate references prove only TKL-side handling; no TKW Candidate lifecycle, approval or Admission is implemented.

##### GOAL

Prepare and export an evidence-grounded raw proposal from local fixtures/manual results, preserving the canonical six-model contracts and uncertain-delivery correlation without invoking external actors.

##### TRIGGER

KnowledgeWorker requests project-local fixture/manual-result execution with an explicit fixturePath and empty storeDirectory.

##### MAIN FLOW

###### local_preparation

1. Validate the UTF-8 fixture and verify that the explicitly selected local store is empty.
2. Seed exact versioned Resources, Evidence and Context with external binding metadata and the existing-information baseline.
3. Fix the Run inputs and existing-information baseline, preserving retained/reference-only content and known/unknown provenance.
4. Import the supplied deterministic/manual preparation result with explicit processor, status and failures.
5. Persist the Run and PreparedMaterial version together through the accepted local atomic/CAS boundary.
6. Compose the immutable producer-key RawCandidateProposal from the persisted material and its exact Run/evidence lineage.
7. Reserve delivery durably before invoking the local result fixture with the supplied correlation and producer/proposal key.
8. Record the fixture Unknown outcome and perform same-key query/retry with exact proposal/correlation handling; any confirmed receipt/Candidate refs remain fixture assertions.
9. Export canonical preparation-bundle JSON, derived PreparedMaterial Markdown and proposal request JSON from persisted values.
10. Return the actual persisted report; later native success carries exact LocalFlowJson.encodeReport output in FixtureExecutionResult.reportJson and expected errors retain structured LocalError/framework failure handling.

