# ACTOR

## KnowledgeWorker

### KIND

human

### DESCRIPTION

A person requesting local preparation and examining evidence-grounded raw proposals.

## TextusKnowledgeWorkbench

### KIND

external

### DESCRIPTION

Modeled future receiver owning Candidate formation, editing, review/approval and Admission. Local fixture outcomes implement no external operation or lifecycle.

## ResourceProvider

### KIND

external

### DESCRIPTION

Modeled future resource/evidence provider. This scenario uses project-local fixtures and implements no provider operation.

## KnowledgeProcessor

### KIND

external

### DESCRIPTION

Modeled future preparation processor. This scenario imports deterministic/manual results and implements no external processing operation.

# VALUE

## FixtureExecutionCommand
- input-kind :: COMMAND

### ATTRIBUTE

| name           | type   | multiplicity |
|----------------|--------|--------------|
| fixturePath    | string | 1            |
| storeDirectory | string | 1            |

## FixtureExecutionResult

### ATTRIBUTE

| name       | type   | multiplicity |
|------------|--------|--------------|
| reportJson | string | 1            |

# SERVICE

## LocalPreparationService

### SUMMARY

Execute the persisted local fixture preparation and proposal flow.

### DESCRIPTION

LocalPreparationService accepts explicit fixturePath and storeDirectory strings through executeFixture. The fixture is read as UTF-8 and the selected store must be fresh. Successful execution persists revisions and derived exports and returns exact report JSON; failures preserve structured code, message, write outcome and observed revision. This service uses local fixture/manual results and supplies no live external integration guarantee.

### OPERATION

#### executeFixture

##### SUMMARY

Run one UTF-8 fixture into a fresh explicit local store and return its persisted report.

##### DESCRIPTION

fixturePath identifies the UTF-8 local-flow v1 fixture; storeDirectory identifies the fresh local store/output directory. Execution persists the accepted preparation/proposal flow and writes preparation-bundle.json, prepared-material.md and proposal-request.json. FixtureExecutionResult.reportJson carries the exact LocalFlowJson.encodeReport output, including persisted revision and export paths. An initialized store is refused; expected failures retain structured LocalError, including whether writes were NotApplied, Applied or Unknown. Projection or report failures can follow committed state. Runtime cleanup removes only owned temporary bootstrap files and never deletes the fixture or store. Receipt and Candidate references remain fixture assertions; no live provider or downstream acceptance is established.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

FixtureExecutionCommand

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

FixtureExecutionResult

# ENTITY

## LocalPreparationSession

### ATTRIBUTE

| name   | type     | multiplicity |
|--------|----------|--------------|
| id     | entityid | 1            |
| status | int      | 1            |

### StateMachine

#### PreparationProposalWorkflow

##### State

